// GENERATED by scripts/merge-content.js — do not edit by hand.
export const NPCS = [{"appearance":{"shirt":"#7b3f9e","pants":"#3a3a4a","hat":"#e8c547","skin":"#d9a06b","hair":"#c0c0c8"},"lines":["Willowbrook was founded on three things: timber, tides, and a truly stubborn refusal to move somewhere drier.","I've proposed a Founders' Day fishing derby every year for nine years. This year the budget committee finally blinked. It's happening.","If anyone asks, the statue in the square is holding a sword. It is absolutely not a very large herring.","The bakery says something keeps rattling the grate out back at night. I told them it's raccoons. Please let it be raccoons.","Between us? The town charter has a clause about a 'glowing grotto' up past the falls. Nobody's amended it out. Nobody's dared.","A mayor's job is ninety percent handshakes and ten percent apologizing to the lighthouse keeper.","Catch something record-worthy and I'll shake your hand at the derby. Around here, that's basically knighthood."],"greeting":"Welcome to Willowbrook! Mind the gulls — they're bolder than the tax code.","zone":"town","id":"mayor-marigold","name":"Mayor Bea Marigold","role":"Mayor of Willowbrook","personality":"Warm, relentlessly civic-minded, and one ribbon-cutting away from carpal tunnel.","shop":null},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#2e4a3d","pants":"#1f2430","hat":null,"skin":"#8a5a38","hair":"#1a1a1a"},"lines":["The vault is carved into the old harbor bedrock. Nothing gets in, nothing gets out. Mostly nothing gets out.","Deposit your earnings before you sail. The sea holds a well-documented lien on optimists.","I once appraised a pearl from the abyssal trench. I still keep the lights on at home. All of them.","Compound interest is like fishing: patience, discipline, and knowing when something is too good to be a real bite.","Chowder sat on my ledger for three hours yesterday. The numbers balanced for the first time all month. I have questions.","Old Halbert deposits the same lucky coin every spring and withdraws it every autumn. I've stopped charging him the fee.","No, I will not accept fish as collateral. Again."],"greeting":"Welcome to the Willowbrook Vault. Your coin is safe. Your secrets, safer.","zone":"town","id":"banker-sterling","name":"Prudence Sterling","role":"Vault Keeper, Willowbrook Bank","personality":"Precise, dry as a receipt, and secretly sentimental about her regulars.","shop":null,"banker":true},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#e07b39","pants":"#4a3728","hat":"#f5f0e6","skin":"#c68e5e","hair":"#5a3a22"},"lines":["Your island, anywhere you like. Meadow pond sunrise? Glacier lake hush? Volcanic hot spring with complimentary steam? Say the word.","Relocation is painless. The portal does all the work. Well — painless for you. The portal complains constantly.","Hot tip: island plots near the coral reef appreciate every time somebody catches something iridescent.","I once moved a client's island out to the trench overlook. He moved back within the week. Said the dark kept looking at him.","Location, location, migration. Fish move with the seasons — the smart angler's island moves with the fish.","Between us, there's a plot registered near a 'luminous cavern' upriver. The paperwork's older than the town. I'd kill to broker it.","No refunds on ocean views. The ocean was there when you signed.","The sewer-adjacent plots are shockingly affordable. Shockingly."],"greeting":"Marlowe Keys, island relocation! Tired of your view? I can fix your view.","zone":"town","id":"broker-marlowe","name":"Marlowe Keys","role":"Island Broker","personality":"Fast-talking portal realtor who genuinely believes every view can be improved.","shop":null,"broker":true},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#8a6d3b","pants":"#5c4a2e","hat":"#3e5c3a","skin":"#b07a4f","hair":"#7a5230"},"lines":["A worm on the hook is worth two in the compost. That's free wisdom. The worms are not free.","Deep-sea fish won't look twice at a garden worm. You want glowshrimp for that. Don't ask where I get glowshrimp.","The kids keep buying my cheapest maggots and 'racing' them. I don't have the heart to explain maggots.","Something in the harbor canals has been stripping hooks clean all week. Whatever it is, it's picky and it's smart.","Swamp leeches: horrible to handle, irresistible to catfish. Life's about tradeoffs.","I sell bait to the sewer hermit at a discount. Partly kindness, partly because he pays in coins from centuries I don't recognize.","You didn't hear it from me, but chum works wonders off the old rig. The foreman pretends to disapprove."],"greeting":"Fresh worms, day-old worms, and worms of mysterious provenance. What'll it be?","zone":"town","id":"bait-maude","name":"Maude Grubb","role":"Bait Shop Owner","personality":"Gruffly practical worm merchant with dirt under her nails and gossip behind her teeth.","shop":"bait"},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#3a5f8a","pants":"#2b2b2b","hat":null,"skin":"#e8b88a","hair":"#8a3b1e"},"lines":["A rod should feel like an argument you're winning. If it feels like an argument you're losing, that's a snapped rod.","Willow heartwood for rivers, whale-bone core for the deep. Anything abyssal, you want something that doesn't mind the pressure. Or the whispers.","Halbert's old rod hangs on my wall. He won't sell it and I won't stop asking. It's tradition now.","Did a repair for the lighthouse keeper once. The rod came back smelling of storms and never cast straight in fair weather again.","Test your drag before the glacier lakes. The fish up there fight cold and quiet, then all at once.","Someone brought me a rod they fished out of the grate behind the bakery. Fine craftsmanship. Older than the bakery. Older than bread, possibly.","The reef will eat cheap tackle alive. Coral has opinions.","I name every rod I sell. The warranty is void if you rename them something stupid."],"greeting":"Every rod in here has a soul. Some have two. Browse gently.","zone":"town","id":"rods-castwell","name":"Reed Castwell","role":"Rod Dealer","personality":"Reverent craftsman who treats every rod like a rescue animal looking for the right home.","shop":"rods"},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#b8452e","pants":"#6e5a3a","hat":"#8f7635","skin":"#f2c9a1","hair":"#d97b28"},"lines":["Lures, bobbers, sonar bells, hook-warmers for the glacier lakes — if it clips onto a line, I've built it. Or exploded it.","My depth-gauge works perfectly all the way down to the trench. Past that, it just displays a tiny picture of a question mark.","The glow-lure was inspired by moss from a cave upriver. I only ever got one sample. I would pay handsomely for more. HANDSOMELY.","Fishing the rig? Take the magnet clamp. Metal fish, metal debris, metal everything out there. Half of it's still warm.","Don't buy the self-hooking hook. I mean, it's for sale, but don't buy it. We've lost three ceiling fans.","The sewer hermit trades me the strangest little gears. Pre-Willowbrook make. Whoever built down there was better at this than me. Don't tell him I said that.","A bell attachment that only rings for rare fish! Current version rings for rare fish and also gulls. Working on it."],"greeting":"Careful where you step — half my inventions are on the floor and a third of those bite.","zone":"town","id":"tinker-tilly","name":"Tilly Sprocket","role":"Attachment Tinkerer","personality":"Caffeinated inventor whose workshop failures are at least as popular as her successes.","shop":"attachments"},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#5a3e7a","pants":"#33402e","hat":"#2e6b4f","skin":"#9c6b43","hair":"#3b2a4a"},"lines":["Bite tonic, lungroot brew for the deep dives, chill-balm for glacier work. Everything's fresh. Everything's mostly legal.","The volcanic hot springs are basically a potion I didn't have to brew. Soak there before a big catch. Trust me.","My best batch needs luminous cave moss, and I have exactly one supplier: a cat. Payment is sardines. The margins are terrible.","Do NOT drink the abyssal calm draught topside. You'll be relaxed in ways this town isn't ready for.","Swamp water is two-thirds of my ingredients and all of my complaints.","The baker swears her sourdough starter growled at her. I sold her a soothing tea. For her, not the starter. The starter is on its own.","A good potion is like a good cast: timing, patience, and being honest about what's in your bucket.","The sewer hermit's cough tincture is ready. If you're passing the grate behind the bakery, tell him. He tips in mystery."],"greeting":"Come in, come in. Mind the fumes — the purple ones are friendly.","zone":"town","id":"brewer-nettle","name":"Sage Nettle","role":"Potion Brewer","personality":"Serene herbalist who speaks about volatile chemistry the way others discuss the weather.","shop":"potions"},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#c9b458","pants":"#4a4238","hat":null,"skin":"#e8b88a","hair":"#8c8c94"},"lines":["Four hundred and twelve documented species in these waters, and I've eaten — catalogued! Catalogued nearly all of them.","Every fish you register in the dex is a footnote in history. Some footnotes bite.","The glowing cave upriver hosts a bioluminescent species that ignores every known lure. It responds only to... something. I've narrowed it down to 'something.'","There are sewer specimens beneath this town found nowhere else in the world. Science demands someone crawl behind that bakery. Science, notably, is not volunteering me.","The abyssal trench entries in my dex are all in Halbert's handwriting. He won't discuss numbers 388 through 391. Not even for pie.","A juvenile reef wrasse changes color eleven times before adulthood. Teenagers, eh?","If you catch anything with the wrong number of eyes, do not release it. Bring it here. Bring it here FIRST.","My rival at the capital academy insists the glacier lakes are barren. Wonderful. More lakes for us."],"greeting":"Ah! An angler with functioning boots. Come, come — what have you caught? SHOW ME.","zone":"town","id":"professor-gill","name":"Professor Finley Gill","role":"Fish Dex Professor","personality":"Boundlessly enthusiastic ichthyologist who has definitely tasted specimens he shouldn't have.","shop":null},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#1f3a5c","pants":"#2b2f38","hat":"#f5f0e6","skin":"#7a4b2e","hair":"#2e2e2e"},"lines":["Reef run's calm, deep sea's honest, the rig's ugly, and the trench... the trench is on the menu because people keep asking.","I've crossed the trench route ninety times. On the ninetieth I stopped counting. Felt like it was counting back.","The rig foreman's good people. Strange people, but good. Bring her coffee and she'll tell you where the metal-eaters school.","Weather out here has moods, not patterns. Anyone who tells you otherwise sells umbrellas.","Morag's light has saved my hull more times than my own steering has. Never sail on a night she's grumpy.","A kid stowed away in my bait cooler last spring, trying to reach the reef. Fined her parents one pie. Best pie I ever confiscated.","The deep sea doesn't hate you. It just doesn't know you're there. Keep it that way.","You want a real secret? The sea is mostly water. The rest of it, you earn."],"greeting":"Ferry leaves when I finish this coffee. Reef, deep sea, the rig, or the trench — pick your poison.","zone":"docks","id":"captain-salt","name":"Captain Ines Salt","role":"Dock Captain and Ferry Master","personality":"Unflappable ferry captain who treats the open ocean like a coworker she has learned to respect.","shop":null},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#6e7b6a","pants":"#4f463a","hat":"#4a5c38","skin":"#b07a4f","hair":"#e8e8e8"},"lines":["Forty years on the water and the fish still surprise me. That's not humility, that's fish for you.","I sell rope, tinned beans, lamp oil, and boot wax. Everything a body needs, nothing a body doesn't.","The Great Marlin of '88? True story. The size grows a little every year, but so do I, sideways.","There's a fish in the abyssal trench I hooked once and let go on purpose. Some doors you're glad you didn't open all the way.","The glowing cave? Aye, I've been. Went in with a lantern, came out not needing one. Never told a soul what does the glowing. Won't start today.","Reed keeps trying to buy my old rod off his own wall. Boy, I gave it to the wall.","Fish the hot springs at dawn once in your life. The steam comes off the water like the world's still being decided.","Retirement's fine. The store is quiet, the pension is beans, and the sea and I wave at each other from a respectful distance."],"greeting":"Shop's open. Stories are free with any purchase, and honestly, free without one.","zone":"town","id":"legend-halbert","name":"Halbert 'The Hook' Grey","role":"Retired Fishing Legend, General Store Owner","personality":"Living legend gone pleasantly rusty, equal parts tall tales and hard-won silence.","shop":"general"},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#403a5c","pants":"#26222e","hat":null,"skin":"#f2c9a1","hair":"#4a3626"},"lines":["Titles are earned, notarized, and permanent. Except 'Pondmaster.' We revoke Pondmaster constantly.","Yes, 'Grand Wormwrangler' is a real title. No, I don't make the rules. I merely emboss them.","Someone filed for 'Trench Whisperer' last month. The paperwork came back damp. I approved it immediately and asked no questions.","The rarest title on record is held by a cat. I've said too much.","Every title has requirements. 'Sewer Sovereign,' for instance, requires deeds performed beneath the bakery that I am legally discouraged from describing.","Halbert holds eleven titles and uses none of them. Some men waste greatness on modesty.","Correct posture, correct forms, correct fish. In that order, and no other order will do.","I once held the title 'Junior Assistant Registrar.' We all start somewhere."],"greeting":"Willowbrook Registrar of Titles. State your achievement and I'll see if it's earned you a name.","zone":"town","id":"registrar-quill","name":"Registrar Ambrose Quill","role":"Registrar of Titles","personality":"Fastidious bureaucrat who wields an embossing stamp with the gravity of a crown.","shop":null},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#d9863f","pants":"#d9863f","hat":null,"skin":"#e8a05c","hair":"#c96f2e"},"lines":["Mrow.","...","Prrrrrb.","The grate behind the bakery opens at low tide. Anyway. Meow.","Mrrp?","*stares at the harbor with the expression of something owed money*","*sits on the registrar's paperwork, radiating authority*","Mao."],"greeting":"Mrrp.","zone":"town","id":"cat-chowder","name":"Chowder","role":"Cat (Allegedly)","personality":"Inscrutable, well-fed, and rumored to hold strong opinions about the trench.","shop":null},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#d94f4f","pants":"#3a5f8a","hat":"#e8c547","skin":"#e8b88a","hair":"#5a3a22"},"lines":["Nan says there's a monster in the canal by the fish market. I say it's TWO monsters. We're doing research.","We found a glowy rock upriver! Pip licked it. Pip is fine. Mostly fine. His tongue glows a little.","The baker chased us off the grate out back AGAIN. Which means there's DEFINITELY treasure down there.","Captain Salt let us ring the ferry bell once. Best day of my LIFE.","Old Halbert says the trench fish have their own kings. Nan didn't sleep for a week. Worth it.","We're saving up for a rod from Mr. Castwell. So far we have nine coins and a really good button.","Chowder talked to me once. Everyone says I dreamed it. Chowder knows what he said."],"greeting":"Race you to the docks! Okay, you won. Rematch!","zone":"town","id":"kids-pip-nan","name":"Pip & Nan","role":"Local Kids","personality":"Inseparable twin menaces powered by rumors, dares, and exactly nine coins.","shop":null},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#8f8f5a","pants":"#3c3c46","hat":"#2b3a4a","skin":"#c68e5e","hair":"#d8d8d8"},"lines":["The light's turned every night for a hundred and six years. Sixty of those were mine. The lens and I are in a committed relationship.","On clear nights I can see the rig burning its little lights out there like a rude constellation.","Storms don't sneak. They announce. You just have to be high enough up to hear the invitation.","There's a green glow up the river valley some nights. Not fire, not foxfire. The lens shows me everything and explains nothing.","The mayor asked if I get lonely. I said I have the gulls, the light, and a strongly worded relationship with the fog.","Ships used to wreck on the reef before my grandmother took this post. Her logbook's last line reads: 'Not on my watch.' Runs in the family.","Some nights something big passes the harbor mouth, below the waterline, running dark. It never comes in. Manners, I suppose."],"greeting":"You climbed all this way? Then you can help me polish the lens. Talk while you buff.","zone":"town","id":"keeper-morag","name":"Keeper Morag","role":"Lighthouse Keeper","personality":"Weathered sentinel who talks to the fog and, worryingly, gets answers.","shop":null},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#4a4a3a","pants":"#3a332a","hat":"#5c5244","skin":"#9c6b43","hair":"#6e6e66"},"lines":["The tunnels under Willowbrook are older than Willowbrook. Somebody fished down there before there was an 'up here.'","Best way in? Grate behind the bakery, at low tide. Bring a light, and mind the third rung — it's decorative.","The fish down there have adapted. To what, I've stopped asking.","I pay Maude for bait in old coins. She thinks they're strange. They think SHE'S strange. Coins talk more than you'd think.","The bakery drops day-olds through the grate on Sundays. Finest breakfast arrangement in town, and neither of us has ever said a word about it.","There's a door down deep with no handle and warm hinges. I don't knock. It hasn't either. We respect each other.","Sunlight's overrated. It's just the one light, and you can't even adjust it.","Tilly's little gears? Found 'em in the silt by the old cistern. Plenty more where those came from, for them as isn't fussy about damp."],"greeting":"Eh? Oh. Surface folk. You're standing in my skylight.","zone":"town","id":"hermit-dregs","name":"Dregs","role":"Sewer Hermit","personality":"Cheerfully subterranean recluse who considers the entire town his ceiling.","shop":null},{"appearance":{"shirt":"#b35a2e","pants":"#3a3f4a","hat":"#e8c547","skin":"#8a5a38","hair":"#2e2620"},"lines":["This rig pumped oil for thirty years. Now it mostly pumps rust and attracts the weirdest fish in three seas.","Metal-eaters school under the south pylon at dusk. They like the taste of the anodes. Cheaper than repainting, honestly.","Captain Salt brings the ferry and my coffee. In that order of importance? No comment.","Something big scrapes the pilings some nights. Long, slow, patient. The rig groans back. I let them talk.","Storm season, the whole platform sings. E-flat, mostly. You get used to it. You even get to missing it.","Head office forgot this rig exists. Best thing that ever happened to it.","Drop a line down the moon pool if you're brave. Straight shot to deep water. What comes up has never once been boring.","The trench is two miles that way and about six miles down. Even my nightmares pack a lunch for that trip."],"greeting":"Watch the catwalks, keep your line off the machinery, and we'll get along fine.","zone":"rig","id":"foreman-cinder","name":"Foreman Vessa Cinder","role":"Oil Rig Foreman","personality":"Deadpan caretaker of a decommissioned rig she refuses to admit she loves.","shop":null}];
